1,Roon language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roon_language,"July 24, 2025 - Roon (Ron) is an Austronesian language spoken in West Papua Province, Indonesia.",Roon,Austronesian
2,Ministry of Culture-Austronesian Music and Cultural Exchange,https://www.moc.gov.tw/en/cp.aspx?n=443,"I noticed that there is no literature on the bamboo drums in the past, but I saw the bamboo drums formerly at the Tainan University of the Arts and took some photos of them. So I am very proud of it. The bamboo drums are very much like the ones in the North of the Philippines, and it is the evidence that Taiwan is the origin of the Austronesians. The other musical instrument is the Jew's harp.",Roon,Austronesian
3,Roon - Music Player & Library Management Software | Free Trial,https://roon.app/en/,"Roon brings all your music together and adds tons of data – bios, reviews, photos, lyrics, tour dates, and cross-linked credits for performers, songwriters, producers, engineers, and composers.",Roon,Austronesian
4,Roon Music Experience - Rich Metadata & Music Discovery Platform,https://roon.app/en/music,"Roon identifies your music files and streams, and then overlays a ton of rich metadata to add context to what you're listening to.",Roon,Austronesian
5,What is Roon? How the music platform works and what devices are Roon Ready | What Hi-Fi?,https://www.whathifi.com/advice/roon-everything-you-need-to-know,"September 11, 2024 - It could also be a NAS (Network Attached Storage) drive, installable with the Roon Core server software, or a dedicated music server such as Roon's own Roon Nucleus One ($500 / approx £400 / approx AU$780) or flagship Roon Nucleus Titan ($3699 / approx £2900 / approx AU$5600), which naturally have the software pre-installed.",Roon,Austronesian
